.Dd August 22, 2026
.Dt LLAMA-MODEL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm llama-model
.Nd manage and run local GGUF models with llama-server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm show
.Ar ALIAS
.Nm
.Cm add
.Ar ALIAS MODEL_GGUF
.Op Ar MMPROJ_GGUF
.Nm
.Cm remove
.Ar ALIAS
.Op Fl -force
.Nm
.Cm run
.Ar ALIAS
.Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
.Nm
.Cm command
.Ar ALIAS
.Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
.Nm
.Cm start
.Ar ALIAS
.Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Brq Ar ALIAS | Fl -all
.Nm
.Cm restart
.Brq Ar ALIAS | Fl -all
.Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
.Nm
.Cm logs
.Ar ALIAS
.Op Fl f | Fl -follow
.Op Fl n Ar LINES
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl -running
.Op Ar ALIAS
.Nm
.Op Fl v | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a POSIX
.Xr sh 1
wrapper around llama.cpp's
.Xr llama-server 1 .
It gives local GGUF model files short, stable aliases and assembles the
right
.Xr llama-server 1
invocation \(em model path, mmproj path, and layered argument files \(em
for each alias.
.Pp
Each alias lives under
.Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT Ns Pa /ALIAS
as a directory containing a symbolic link
.Pa model.gguf
(and, for a vision model, a second link
.Pa mmproj.gguf )
pointing at the real, long-named downloaded file.
.Nm
never copies model data; it only manages links and small per-alias metadata
files.
.Pp
Anywhere
.Ar ALIAS
is accepted, a plain number is also accepted as the 1-based index shown by
.Cm list
or
.Cm status .
That index is positional and can shift as aliases are added or removed.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
List every alias in the catalog, one per line, prefixed with its 1-based
index.
.It Cm show Ar ALIAS
Print the alias's resolved model path, mmproj path (or
.Dq (none) ) ,
and the path to its per-model
.Pa server.args
file, if any.
.It Cm add Ar ALIAS MODEL_GGUF Op Ar MMPROJ_GGUF
Create
.Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT Ns Pa /ALIAS
and symlink
.Ar MODEL_GGUF
to
.Pa model.gguf
inside it (and
.Ar MMPROJ_GGUF ,
if given, to
.Pa mmproj.gguf ) .
.Ar MODEL_GGUF
and
.Ar MMPROJ_GGUF
are resolved to their canonical path before linking.
A
.Fl -port
line is written to the new alias's
.Pa server.args ,
one past the highest
.Fl -port
already in use across the global args file and every other alias, so newly
added models do not collide on the default port.
.It Cm remove Ar ALIAS Op Fl -force
Delete
.Ar ALIAS Ns 's
catalog directory, i.e. its
.Pa model.gguf
and
.Pa mmproj.gguf
links and
.Pa server.args ,
not the underlying downloaded files.
Refuses while the alias is running
unless
.Fl -force
is given, in which case it is stopped first.
.It Cm run Ar ALIAS Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
Assemble the argument list for
.Ar ALIAS
and
.Xr exec 3
.Ev LLAMA_SERVER
in place of the wrapper, so signals and exit status pass through correctly
under
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Pa rc.d ,
or a terminal multiplexer.
Runs in the foreground.
.It Cm command Ar ALIAS Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
Build the identical argument list as
.Cm run
but print the shell-quoted, ready-to-paste
.Ev LLAMA_SERVER
invocation instead of executing it.
Useful for inspecting what would run, or for copying into another
supervisor.
.It Cm start Ar ALIAS Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
Run
.Ar ALIAS
detached in the background, redirecting stdout and stderr to
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.log
and recording its process ID in
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.pid
and its host:port in
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.addr .
Fails if the alias is already running.
.It Cm stop Brq Ar ALIAS | Fl -all
Send
.Dv SIGTERM
to the running alias's process and wait for it to exit, removing the
.Pa server.pid
and
.Pa server.addr
files.
With
.Fl -all
in place of
.Ar ALIAS ,
stops every alias currently reported as running.
.It Cm restart Brq Ar ALIAS | Fl -all Op Ar LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS ...
Stop the alias if it is running, then start it again with the given
arguments.
With
.Fl -all ,
restarts every alias currently reported as running.
.It Cm logs Ar ALIAS Op Fl f | Fl -follow Op Fl n Ar LINES
Print the last
.Ar LINES
lines (default 50) of
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.log .
.Fl f
or
.Fl -follow
follows the file like
.Xr tail 1 Ns 's
.Fl f
flag.
.It Cm status Op Fl -running Op Ar ALIAS
Print a table of alias, run state, process ID, port, and address.
With no
.Ar ALIAS ,
lists every alias; with
.Ar ALIAS ,
shows only that one.
.Fl -running
restricts the listing to running aliases and may not be combined with an
.Ar ALIAS
argument.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the
.Nm
version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Configuration is layered and sourced as shell code, not parsed:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/llama-models.conf
(or
.Pa ~/.config/llama-models.conf
if
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset), or the file named by
.Ev LLAMA_MODELS_CONFIG ,
is dot-sourced if present.
It may set
.Ev LLAMA_SERVER ,
.Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT ,
and
.Ev LLAMA_GLOBAL_ARGS .
.It
Any of those left unset fall back to hardcoded defaults; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.El
.Pp
Environment variables already set before invoking
.Nm
take precedence over the config file, since the file assigns with
.Ev VAR Ns = Ns \&${ Ns Ev VAR Ns :- Ns Ar default Ns } .
.Sh ARGUMENT FILES
.Ev LLAMA_GLOBAL_ARGS
(default
.Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT Ns Pa /server.args )
and each alias's
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.args
list
.Xr llama-server 1
arguments, one per line: an option and its value are two separate lines.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Sq #
are ignored.
One argument per line is what lets an argument's value contain spaces.
.Pp
.Cm run
and
.Cm command
assemble arguments in this precedence order, later winning, since
.Xr llama-server 1
uses last-flag-wins semantics and each source is appended after the
previous:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Ev LLAMA_GLOBAL_ARGS
\(em options for every model.
.It
.Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.args
\(em per-model overrides.
.It
Extra arguments passed on the command line after
.Ar ALIAS
\(em highest precedence.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "LLAMA_MODELS_CONFIG"
.It Ev LLAMA_SERVER
Path to the
.Xr llama-server 1
executable.
Default:
.Pa ~/src/github/ggml-org/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server .
.It Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT
Path to the catalog directory.
Default:
.Pa ~/models/catalog .
.It Ev LLAMA_GLOBAL_ARGS
Path to the global arguments file.
Default:
.Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT Ns Pa /server.args .
.It Ev LLAMA_MODELS_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file to source.
Default:
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/llama-models.conf
or
.Pa ~/.config/llama-models.conf .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "ALIAS/server.addr" -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/llama-models.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Ev LLAMA_MODEL_ROOT Ns Pa /server.args
Default global arguments file.
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /model.gguf
Symlink to the model file for
.Ar ALIAS .
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /mmproj.gguf
Symlink to the multimodal projector file for
.Ar ALIAS ,
if any.
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.args
Per-model argument overrides for
.Ar ALIAS .
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.pid
Process ID of a running
.Ar ALIAS ,
written by
.Cm start
and removed by
.Cm stop .
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.addr
Host and port of a running
.Ar ALIAS .
.It Ar ALIAS Ns Pa /server.log
Combined stdout/stderr log of a background
.Ar ALIAS .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits 2 if invoked with no command, and 1 on any other usage error or
operational failure (unknown alias, invalid alias name, alias already or
not running, etc.).
.Sh EXAMPLES
Add a text-only model and a vision-language model, then inspect and run one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
llama-model add llama8 ~/models/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf
llama-model add qwen-vl \e
    ~/models/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf \e
    ~/models/mmproj-Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct-f16.gguf

llama-model list
llama-model show qwen-vl
llama-model command qwen-vl
llama-model run qwen-vl
.Ed
.Pp
Override an argument for one invocation; overrides passed on the command
line win over both argument files:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
llama-model run llama8 --port 8081 --ctx-size 16384
.Ed
.Pp
Run a model as a background service and inspect it later:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
llama-model start llama8
llama-model status
llama-model logs llama8 -f
llama-model stop llama8
.Ed
.Pp
Swap a model's underlying quantization by repointing its symlink, then
verify before starting it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ln -sfn ~/models/new-long-model-name.gguf \e
    ~/models/catalog/llama8/model.gguf
llama-model show llama8
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr daemon 8
